The tick looks at the drained shares only once the count is past the release.
A share whose account filled would wait a tick longer on the spent queue;
the release lies ahead of the count.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: the release is for a tick already past

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -459,7 +459,7 @@ static void tick_advance(uint32_t ticks)
         }
     }
     nearest_deadline = nearest;
-    if (!tick_before(sched_ticks, nearest_release)) {
+    if (tick_before(nearest_release, sched_ticks)) {
         release();
     }
 }
